BEGIN ARTICLE QUALITY CHECK:

1. Check if articles appear empty or contain minimal text: All articles contain substantial content—ranging from ~150 to over 1,000 words each—including direct quotes, timestamps, named officials, casualty figures, geographic details, diplomatic developments, and contextual analysis. None fall below ~50 words.

2. Paywall indicators: No phrases like “subscribe”, “premium access”, “continue reading”, or login prompts appear in any article body. All content is fully rendered and self-contained.

3. Headlines/URLs only? No — every entry includes a headline *and* a rich, descriptive news body with attribution, chronology, and multi-source perspectives (e.g., Al Jazeera, Guardian, BBC, France 24, Axios, official statements).

4. Truncation: No article ends mid-sentence or cuts off abruptly. Each concludes with a coherent final clause or paragraph; even live-blog entries (#63474) end with a complete dateline and statistic.

✅ All articles are complete, substantive, and analyzable.

