a) **Key Themes Across All Articles**  
- **Migration Policy Overhaul**: Both articles center on the EU’s newly agreed-upon returns regulation — a cornerstone of a multi-year, post-2015-crisis reform of the EU’s asylum and migration system.  
- **Expansion of Coercive Enforcement Tools**: Home raids, extended detention (up to 30 months), offshore “return hubs”, benefit sanctions, lifetime entry bans, and detention of unaccompanied minors/families are all highlighted as novel or significantly expanded powers.  
- **Transatlantic Policy Convergence & Critique**: A dominant framing is the explicit comparison to U.S. ICE under the *second Trump presidency*, with critics accusing the EU of importing “brutal”, “xenophobic”, and “draconian” enforcement models rather than learning from their documented harms.  
- **Political Realignment in the EU**: The 2024 European Parliament elections are identified as a pivotal turning point — the shift rightward enabled center-right (EPP) and far-right groups to jointly override traditional parliamentary safeguards, transforming the Parliament from a “brake” into an enabler of stringent returns policy.  
- **Externalization of Migration Control**: Heavy emphasis on bilateral negotiations with third countries (especially in Africa) to host offshore return hubs — modeled on Italy-Albania — reflects a systemic move to relocate detention and processing outside EU legal jurisdiction and oversight.  
- **Human Rights Erosion Concerns**: Multiple civil society actors (Platform for Cooperation on Undocumented Migrants, International Rescue Committee, Green MEPs) uniformly warn of violations of the EU Charter of Fundamental Rights, risks of refoulement, torture, family separation, and creation of “legal black holes”.

b) **Recurring Names, Places, or Events**  
- **People**: Magnus Brunner (EU Commissioner for Migration, EPP-aligned, architect of proposals); Regina Doherty (EPP Irish MEP, pro-deal spokesperson); Mélissa Camara (Green French MEP, critic); Silvia Carta / Silvia Carter (likely same person — minor spelling variation across sources — advocacy officer/spokesperson for Platform for Cooperation on Undocumented Migrants); Nicholas Ioannides (Cypriot Deputy Migration Minister, rotating Council presidency); Ursula von der Leyen (EC President, EPP coalition).  
- **Organizations/Institutions**: European Commission, European Council, European Parliament (collectively “three-way talks”/“trilogue”); Platform for Cooperation on Undocumented Migrants (Brussels-based NGO); International Rescue Committee; European People’s Party (EPP); Greens/European Green Party; far-right groups (unnamed but referenced as coalition partners with EPP).  
